      "url": "https://www.laconservancy.org/learn/historic-places/chinese-theatre/",
      "inspection": "Primary preservation record actually read. Meyer and Holler1927design;90ftpagoda roof, large columns/wroughtironmasks, bells and stone guardian dogs.2000–2001exteriorrestoration.2013IMAXconversion concerned auditorium. Nominal90ft(27.432m) overall height is a control, not a surveyed plan."
    },
    {
      "url": "https://www.tclchinesetheatres.com/about-us",
      "inspection": "Current official owner page actually read.2013TCLnaming/digitalmarquee/lobbyandseatingupgrade; historicforecourt/golden doors retained. Exterior modeled from2012–2014local photographs, not a claim of current temporary display content."
    },
    {
      "url": "https://www.google.com/maps/@34.10201,-118.34096,20z/data=!3m1!1e3",
      "inspection": "Current aerial actually inspected. Large rectangular rear auditorium, small centered green pagoda entrance and curved open south forecourt bounded by narrow gateway blocks. West neighboring building and massive east Hollywood complex are separate. Main roof has low rectangular equipment/paired diagonal service frames; hidden details are generalized."
    }
